  {
    "id" : "category_ecmascript_codestyle_NoElseReturn",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Unnecessary Else After Return",
    "description" : "This rule detects unnecessary else blocks following an if block that contains a return statement.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 5.5.0\n\nThe else block in a if-else-construct is unnecessary if the `if` block contains a return.\nThen the content of the else block can be put outside.\n\nSee also: &lt;http://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-else-return&gt;\n\nExample(s):\n```\n// Bad:\nif (x) {\n    return y;\n} else {\n    return z;\n}\n\n// Good:\nif (x) {\n    return y;\n}\nreturn z;\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Javascript"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_ecmascript_codestyle_UnnecessaryBlock",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Unnecessary Blocks",
    "description" : "Detects unnecessary blocks in ECMAScript code that do not introduce new variable scope and can be misleading.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 5.0\n\nAn unnecessary Block is present.  Such Blocks are often used in other languages to\nintroduce a new variable scope.  Blocks do not behave like this in ECMAScipt, and using them can\nbe misleading.  Considering removing this unnecessary Block.\n\nExample(s):\n```\nif (foo) {\n    // Ok\n}\nif (bar) {\n    {\n        // Bad\n    }\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Javascript"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_ecmascript_codestyle_UnnecessaryParentheses",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Unnecessary Parentheses",
    "description" : "This rule detects and flags unnecessary parentheses in code expressions that do not affect the evaluation order.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 5.0\n\nUnnecessary parentheses should be removed.\n\nExample(s):\n```\nvar x = 1; // Ok\nvar y = (1 + 1); // Ok\nvar z = ((1 + 1)); // Bad\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Javascript"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_ecmascript_codestyle_UnreachableCode",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Unreachable Code",
    "description" : "Detects code statements that appear after a return, break, continue, or throw statement within a block, which will never be executed.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 5.0\n\nA 'return', 'break', 'continue', or 'throw' statement should be the last in a block. Statements after these\nwill never execute.  This is a bug, or extremely poor style.\n\nExample(s):\n```\n// Ok\nfunction foo() {\n   return 1;\n}\n// Bad\nfunction bar() {\n   var x = 1;\n   return x;\n   x = 2;\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Javascript"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_ecmascript_codestyle_WhileLoopsMustUseBraces",
    "level" : "Info",
