    "title" : "Replace Vector With List",
    "description" : "This rule suggests replacing usage of the legacy Vector class with the newer java.util.List implementations such as ArrayList when thread-safe operations are not required.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 3.4\n\nConsider replacing Vector usages with the newer java.util.ArrayList if expensive thread-safe operations are not required.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic class Foo {\n    void bar() {\n        Vector v = new Vector();\n    }\n}\n```",
