    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Assignment In Operand",
    "description" : "This rule discourages the use of assignments within operands, such as within conditional statements.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 1.03\n\nAvoid assignments in operands; this can make code more complicated and harder to read.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic void bar() {\n    int x = 2;\n    if ((x = getX()) == 3) {\n      System.out.println(\"3!\");\n    }\n}\n```",
