  {
    "id" : "category_java_errorprone_AssignmentToNonFinalStatic",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Assignment To Non-Final Static Fields in Constructors",
    "description" : "Detects assignments to non-final static fields within constructors which can lead to unsafe and unpredictable behavior.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 2.2\n\nIdentifies a possible unsafe usage of a static field.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic class StaticField {\n   static int x;\n   public FinalFields(int y) {\n    x = y; // unsafe\n   }\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
