    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_java_security_InsecureCryptoIv",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "Cryptography",
    "title" : "Avoid Hard Coded Initialization Vector in Cryptographic Operations",
    "description" : "This rule detects usage of hard coded initialization vectors (IVs) in cryptographic operations.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 6.3.0\n\nDo not use hard coded initialization vector in cryptographic operations. Please use a randomly generated IV.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic class Foo {\n    void good() {\n        SecureRandom random = new SecureRandom();\n        byte iv[] = new byte[16];\n        random.nextBytes(bytes);\n    }\n\n    void bad() {\n        byte[] iv = new byte[] { 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, 00, };\n    }\n\n    void alsoBad() {\n        byte[] iv = \"secret iv in here\".getBytes();\n    }\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_jsp_bestpractices_DontNestJsfInJstlIteration",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Nesting JSF Components Inside JSTL Iteration",
    "description" : "Prevents nesting JSF component custom actions inside JSTL iteration tags like <c:forEach>.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 3.6\n\nDo not nest JSF component custom actions inside a custom action that iterates over its body.\n\nExample(s):\n```\n<html>\n  <body>\n    <ul>\n      <c:forEach items='${books}' var='b'>\n        <li> <h:outputText value='#{b}' /> </li>\n      </c:forEach>\n    </ul>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```",
